---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Security and Trust | Prodory" description="How the Prodory website and enquiry process handles your data, and how we approach security in the platforms we build." path="/security/">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[900px] px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Security and trust</h1>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">This website</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 grid list-disc gap-3 pl-5 text-[#4B5563]">
      <li>The site is static. Forms are the only dynamic part, and they post to a same-origin function on the site.</li>
      <li>Enquiries are rate-limited and checked for spam before they are stored.</li>
      <li>We do not run third-party trackers or advertising pixels on this site.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Platforms we build</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 grid list-disc gap-3 pl-5 text-[#4B5563]">
      <li>Access is granted through your identity provider, and changes go through reviewed pull requests.</li>
      <li>Admission policy, secrets management and network policy are defined in code.</li>
      <li>Audit logs are kept for the period your compliance rules require.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-[#4B5563]">Certifications: Prodory does not currently hold third-party security certifications. We will state any certification here only once it is issued.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
